php-vitexsoftware-rbczpremiumapi (1.5.8) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix uncaught RateLimitExceededException crashing consumers on rate-
    limit exhaustion: RateLimitExceededException now extends
    ApiException (code 429) so existing catch(ApiException) blocks catch
    it. Add RBAPI_RATE_MAX_WAIT_SECONDS (default 300) to bound wait-mode
    sleeps, preventing a day-window reset from blocking a caller for up
    to 24h.

 -- vitex <info@vitexsoftware.cz>  Thu, 30 Jul 2026 11:14:38 +0200

php-vitexsoftware-rbczpremiumapi (1.5.7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add opt-in host-wide rate limit (RateLimiter::checkGlobalBeforeRequest(),
    RBAPI_GLOBAL_RATE_LIMIT_PER_SECOND / global_rate_limit_per_second): a
    self-tracked cap on requests per second shared across ALL certificates
    using the same rate limit store, not just the one making the current
    request. Per-certificate enforcement alone cannot see a gateway-level
    limit above the certificate scope (e.g. per source IP or per
    account-holder), since RB's response headers only ever report the
    calling certificate's own remaining quota; many certificates can each
    show plenty of headroom while collectively exceeding such a shared
    limit. Disabled by default (0) since the true scope of RB's gateway
    limit is not documented
  * Add ApiClient/RateLimiter tests for the new global cap
  * Document the global cap in README.md

 -- vitex <info@vitexsoftware.cz>  Sun, 19 Jul 2026 18:17:40 +0200

php-vitexsoftware-rbczpremiumapi (1.5.6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: ApiClient::send() recovers the response from Guzzle's RequestException
    on 4xx/5xx instead of letting it throw before the 429 handling ever runs,
    so a 429 always reaches the rate-limit retry/exception logic
  * Add per-certificate exclusive file locking (RateLimiter::acquireLock/
    releaseLock) around the check-send-update cycle in ApiClient::send(), so
    concurrent processes sharing one certificate (e.g. one task per bank
    account under the same company) serialize instead of racing past stale
    rate-limit counters
  * Add RBAPI_RATE_LIMIT_LOCK_DIR config option / env var for the lock directory
  * Add ApiClientTest and RateLimiter locking tests
  * Document the 429 recovery and locking behavior in README.md
  * Relax guzzlehttp/guzzle back to ^7.4 and guzzlehttp/psr7 back to
    ^1.8 || ^2.4 (previous dependabot PRs #59/#60 had tightened these past
    what bookworm/trixie/jammy/noble/resolute actually package, breaking
    apt installation of the built .deb with unmet dependencies)

 -- vitex <info@vitexsoftware.cz>  Thu, 16 Jul 2026 17:09:25 +0200

